rustchain-claim-portal
======================

This product includes software developed by:

* Scott Boudreaux / Elyan Labs / Scottcjn (RustChain integration)
* The MergeWork contributors (https://github.com/ramimbo/mergework, MIT)

Portions of this software are derived from MergeWork (Copyright (c) 2026
MergeWork contributors), specifically:

  * GitHub OAuth wallet-linking flow (originally `app/auth.py`)
  * The `/me` route pattern for showing balance + linked wallet
  * The "lazy-pay then claim" pattern using `github:<login>` as a placeholder
    account until the contributor provisions a wallet
  * The MCP-server-over-HTTP shape for AI-agent interaction

The original MergeWork LICENSE is preserved at:
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/mergework-MIT.txt

Adapted files carry an attribution header indicating which sections are
ported and how they have been modified for RustChain (Flask vs FastAPI,
ledger-backed-by-chain vs ledger-as-source-of-truth, `RTC` wallet prefix
vs `mrwk1`, calls to RustChain Node 1's `/wallet/transfer` instead of
writing directly to SQLite).

What was NOT ported:
  * MergeWork's issuance model. MergeWork mints MRWK by maintainer label
    application (centralized). RustChain mints RTC only via mined epoch
    rewards on real hardware (Proof of Antiquity). The portal is a
    CLAIM/CLAIM-PAY surface, not a mint surface.
  * MergeWork's SQLite ledger as source-of-truth. In rustchain-claim-portal,
    the SQLite is a cache + identity-mapping; the RustChain node remains
    the authoritative ledger.

